// PARAM: --analysis interval
// The branch transfer's forward feasibility gate, not backward narrowing, is
// what makes this branch dead. Backward narrowing alone cannot: bfilter's Eq
// case inverts "(x < 0) == 1" to an empty target for its left operand, but
// afilter has no narrowing rule for a comparison node, so the empty target is
// dropped and the incoming state survives unchanged. The gate instead
// evaluates the whole condition forward -- interval_tobool of [0,0] answers
// Some False -- and contradicts the selected polarity, so the then-branch has
// no successor at all and its check never reaches the report.
// Example_Guard_Refinement.thy pins both halves of that comparison directly on
// the abstract state.
void main() {
  x := 5;
  if ((x < 0) == 1) {
    __voblint_check(false) // NOWARN (unreachable)
  } else {
    __voblint_check(true) // PROVED
  }
}
